    {
      "id": "claim_0dc6e113492f4afdbaf3f50c8458b0e3",
      "statement": "save_bodyweight_entry is a SECURITY INVOKER Postgres function that requires auth.uid(), re-validates date/weight, takes a per-owner pg_advisory_xact_lock keyed on hashtextextended(user_id,0) to serialize concurrent calendar writes, locks the target entry and destination-date row FOR UPDATE, only deletes an occupied destination row when p_replace_entry_id explicitly matches it (raising unique_violation otherwise), and performs the insert/update and any replacement delete in one transaction; it is revoked from public/anon and granted only to authenticated.",
